{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1564 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "cdf0904794c11ffe126c033d683270789c8515923ca9b0cf1303f9bf3738acc9" :edb/db-before-t 1563 :edb/db-after-t 1564 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534876 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:21:59.398Z" 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186132355 1078 #edb/ref 17592186132356 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186133896 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442249 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186133896 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442250 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186133896 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442252 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186133897 1038 #edb/ref 17592186442251 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186134386 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186134386 1071 "![](images/01/01a5f06674cacca4764f438a8c06f020659f0177a0b74952f40bc9072627ec3f.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C = C_{1}∪C_{2}$, where\n\n- $C_{1}$ is parametrized by $r_{1}(t) = 2t^{2}i - t^{3}j$ for $t ∈ [- 1, 1]$, and\n- $C_{2}$ is parametrized by $r_{2}(t) = 2i + tj$ for $t ∈ [- 1, 1]$.\n\nUse Green's theorem to find the area of the region." 13194139534876 17592186045417 false] [17592186134386 1071 "![](images/01/01a5f06674cacca4764f438a8c06f020659f0177a0b74952f40bc9072627ec3f.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2},$ where \n\n- ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=2{t}^{2}\\,i-{t}^{3}\\,j$ for $t\\in [-1,1],$ and\n\n- ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(t)=2\\,i+t\\,j$ for $t\\in [-1,1].$\n\nUse Green's theorem to find the area of the region." 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186134386 1074 "First, let $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$\n\nOur simple, piecewise-smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0-(-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y=-{∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivatives of ${r}_{1}(t)$ and ${r}_{2}(t)$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\, & {r}_{1}^{′}(t)=4t\\,i-3{t}^{2}\\,j \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\, & {r}_{2}^{′}(t)=j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}}y\\,dx \\\\  & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}}y\\,dx-{∮}_{{C}_{2}}y\\,dx \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-{t}^{3})\\cdot 4t\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}t\\cdot 0\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{4}\\,\\text{d}t-0 \\\\  & =4[\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186442224 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442253 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186442224 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442254 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186442224 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442255 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186442224 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442256 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186442224 1043 #edb/ref 17592186442257 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186442224 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186442224 1045 "Using Green's Theorem to Calculate Area" 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186442224 1046 #edb/ref 17592186442254 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186442224 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186442224 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050567 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186442224 1053 #uuid "5a146ad8-7f02-557a-a03b-2c457ab4ba04" 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186442225 1080 "3{sin}^{3}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t" 13194139534876 17592186045417 true] [17592186442225 1082 #edb/ref 17592186